cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the dataset it produces, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "twstat: recovering tidy data from legacy East Asian statistical tables"
abstract: >-
  A Python package and derived dataset that convert the education, health
  services and poor relief chapters of the Taiwan Province Statistical Abstract
  for the Past Fifty-One Years (1946) from layout-preserving legacy spreadsheets
  into tidy long-format data, with era dates resolved to Gregorian years, the
  reporting convention kept as a separate field, the compilers' own
  missing-value legend preserved, and every value carrying the spreadsheet cell
  it was read from.
authors:
  - family-names: Lo
    given-names: Yu-Cheng
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/peterlo920307/twstat-social"
keywords:
  - digital humanities
  - historical statistics
  - data rescue
  - colonial Taiwan
  - history of education
  - history of public health
references:
  - type: dataset
    title: "臺灣省五十一年來統計提要 (Taiwan Province Statistical Abstract for the Past Fifty-One Years)"
    year: 2006
    authors:
      - name: "Institute of Information Science, Academia Sinica"
    url: "http://twstudy.iis.sinica.edu.tw/twstatistic50/"
    notes: >-
      Digitisation of the 1946 compendium compiled by the Statistical Office of
      the Taiwan Provincial Administrative Executive Office. Source of the raw
      spreadsheets, which are not redistributed here.
